  "body": "# Aphid 0.1.2-dev \u2014 bundled graph algorithms\n\nALGO is now statically bundled alongside FTS, vector, and DuckDB. Graph\nalgorithms run through `Aphid.query/3` without an `INSTALL` or `LOAD` step.\n`Aphid.info/1` reports `[\"algo\", \"duckdb\", \"fts\", \"vector\"]`.\n\nIncluded procedures: PageRank, strongly and weakly connected components,\nKosaraju SCC, Louvain, k-core decomposition, and spanning forest. Project graph\ntables with `PROJECT_GRAPH`, then call the algorithm. The extension guide and\n`examples/algo.exs` provide a complete PageRank example.\n\nIcebug-backed `GDS_*` functions remain disabled. A pinned build-only patch\nremoves the unused OpenMP requirement from the standard algorithms; this release\nadds no icebug, Arrow, or OpenMP runtime dependency. The five hardening fixes\nfrom `0.1.1-dev` remain included.\n\nThe new tests check PageRank, connected-component membership, projection cleanup,\nand the documented example. The other bundled algorithms are not individually\nqualified by these tests. Release verification is recorded in\n`docs/evidence/release-012.md`.\n\nUse `{:aphid, \"== 0.1.2-dev\"}` with Elixir 1.20.0 / OTP 29.0.4. Native archives\nare provided for macOS ARM64 and Linux x86_64/ARM64 with glibc. Keep the bundled\nlicenses and accompanying notices when redistributing native files.\n\nThis is an experimental prerelease. Minimum-system/CPU execution, ALGO sanitizer\ncoverage, broader TSan/Zig allocation checks, and production support remain open.\nExisting releases are unchanged.\n"
